# Netlify redirects.
#
# 1. Old WordPress URLs -> new pages. The live site has been indexed by Google
#    since 2024; without these, every ranking and backlink for those addresses
#    would 404 on launch day. 301 = permanent, which is what passes ranking on.
/aboutus              /about/       301!
/aboutus/             /about/       301!
/product              /products/    301!
/product/             /products/    301!
/get-in-touch         /contact/     301!
/get-in-touch/        /contact/     301!

# 2. The 13 WordPress theme demo posts that were never deleted — photography
#    and branding filler indexed under a coatings domain. Retired, not migrated.
/hello-world/                              /blog/  301!
/cultivating-originality-in-photography/   /blog/  301!
/cultivating-originality-in-photography-dark/ /blog/ 301!
/is-it-time-to-rebrand/                    /blog/  301!
/is-it-time-to-rebrand-2/                  /blog/  301!
/is-it-time-to-rebrand-dark/               /blog/  301!
/simplistic-photo-setup/                   /blog/  301!
/setting-up-the-creativity/                /blog/  301!
/setting-up-the-creativity-2/              /blog/  301!
/endless-road-stories/                     /blog/  301!
/design-to-remember/                       /blog/  301!
/start-unique-experience/                  /blog/  301!
/future-business-ideas/                    /blog/  301!

# 3. The client wrote down /admin-panel; /admin is the real route.
/admin-panel          /admin/        301!
/admin-panel/*        /admin/:splat  301!

# 4. Studio routing. It is a single-page app: /admin/structure/faqPage is
#    handled by JavaScript, not by a file on disk, so every path under /admin
#    must serve the studio shell (200, not a redirect) or refreshing a page
#    inside the admin panel would 404.
#
#    Do NOT add "/admin  /admin/  301!" here. Netlify already normalises
#    trailing slashes, so that rule and Netlify's own normalisation redirect
#    to each other forever — ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS on the admin panel.
#    Tried and reverted. The rewrite below covers /admin and everything under it.
/admin/*              /admin/index.html  200
